13. Shared hit resolver

The new system must be generic.

CombatSystem.applyHit() must not contain checks such as:

if (def.id === 'ba1')
if (fighter.id === '0001')
if (technique.id === 'rasenRush')

The shared resolution path should work from hit data.

A clean conceptual sequence is:

const launchPointBefore = target.combat.launchPoint;
const damage = ...; // full or blocked/chip damage according to existing defense rules
target.combat.launchPoint =
  Math.max(0, launchPointBefore + damage);
const launchPointAfter = target.combat.launchPoint;
const launchStrength =
  def.baseLaunch * launchPointAfter;
const launch = resolveDirectionalLaunch(
  launchStrength,
  def.directionalLaunch,
  facing
);

Then apply the resulting velocity according to the existing hit/block rules.

Melee, projectiles, summoned clones, and charged-technique hits should all travel through the same underlying launch calculation.

