44. Expected implementation shape

The finished architecture should be understandable at a glance.

A normal hit should conceptually reduce to:

const damage = resolveDamage(...);
const launchPointBefore = target.combat.launchPoint;
target.combat.launchPoint += damage;
const launchPointAfter = target.combat.launchPoint;
const launchStrength =
  def.baseLaunch * launchPointAfter;
const finalLaunch =
  directionalLaunchVector(
    def.directionalLaunch,
    launchStrength,
    facing
  );
applyVelocity(target, finalLaunch);

with Block modifying the resolved physical launch afterward.

That is the core system.

Do not make it more complicated than necessary.

